# Preserve LF line endings for all tracked files, on every platform.
#
# Why: manifest.json contains SHA-256 hashes of every distributed file. Those
# hashes are computed once (via scripts/generate-manifest.sh) and verified at
# install time by serious-update. If git's core.autocrlf converts files to
# CRLF on Windows checkout, every hash check fails and 0 files distribute.
#
# `* -text` tells git: treat every file as binary (no eol conversion, ever).
# This is safe — none of the toolkit's tracked files are platform-specific
# in a way that requires native line endings.
* -text
